  <name>QuixiCore</name>
  <summary>Native Rust desktop workspace for AI, with a working Linux platform layer</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.volkdude85">
    <name>volkdude85</name>
  </developer>
  <description>
    <p>
      A desktop workspace that runs AI models locally or over the internet, keeps its memory in a
      folder of markdown you own, and works on your own files.
    </p>
    <p>
      An AI-assisted build, said plainly: the Linux platform layer was written by an agent under my
      direction. I set the behaviour, read every patch, and test every build on real hardware. Built
      by a disabled developer who is a good technician and a bad typist.
    </p>
    <p>
      This build carries a Linux platform layer the upstream release leaves as silent no-ops outside
      macOS: screen capture through the KDE ScreenShot2 portal in-process, Wayland clipboard access,
      synthetic input through ydotool, file and folder pickers, display listing, cursor position and
      application launching.
    </p>
  </description>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.volkdude85.QuixiDesk.desktop</launchable>
